# Vendored upstream data — re-fetch with tools/fetch_data.sh, never commit
vendor/
build/
dist/
.vercel/
.env
.env.local

# Generated assets. Both are derived from vendor/ and reproducible:
# tools/build_meshes.py writes generated/, tools/web_pack.py selects web/.
assets/generated/
assets/web/
# LDraw's primitives, copied from vendor/ldraw/p by tools/export.sh into
# every build (PartForge.SHIPPED).
assets/ldraw/p/
godot/assets/parts/
*.pck
*.wasm

# Godot
.godot/
.import/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Node
node_modules/

# Editors / OS
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
shots/
models/design.ldr
# The design bench's runs: designs, renders, fetched photographs, the judge's
# replies. Its summary is docs/DESIGN_SCORES.md; photographs are not ours to commit.
bench/results/
.vercel
tools/web/node_modules/
tools/web/package-lock.json

# Web assets are served, not imported. web/.gdignore keeps the engine out.
*.import
# Except these, which say "keep": the cursor and control pictures ship as
# SVG source and are drawn at run time at the density wanted (src/ui/icons.gd).
# Without the file a fresh checkout imports them as textures, the export
# packs the texture and not the SVG, and every cursor quietly falls back.
!assets/ui/**/*.svg.import
# And the render's HDR panoramas, imported at 512 x 256 (process/size_limit):
# without it a fresh checkout packs them at four times the size.
!assets/hdri/*.hdr.import

# Scratch probes. A review agent that tests its own hypothesis by
# writing a probe and running it is doing the right thing — this
# project's rule is to measure rather than reason — but those files are
# working notes, not the suite. Twenty-six of them reached main because
# the commits that followed used "git add -A".
src/dev/_*
